100 level game anyway, but leave me some levels
whose walls I can cheerfully pick-axe flat one by
one (not just a short-cut, the whole level, to be
tidy).

>> and pudding farming hindered,

Why on earth do people who'd never have the patience
to do this, continue to whine about it being
available for the rest of us to enjoy, so
repetitively? You'd think people who hate repetitive
tasks would have long ago given up on this one.

> For a single user system that's no problem, but if
